        "abstract": "Digital image scrambling is often used in encryption technology and information hiding technology. In practical application, the pixel distribution of the scrambling image is expected to be uniform. In this paper, we propose the evaluation method of digital image scrambling degree, then propose the construction method of arbitrary subspace which is applied in the proposed evaluation method. We perform two sets of experiments on seven images to verify the performance of the proposed construction of arbitrary subspace and the proposed evaluation method of digital image scrambling degree, respectively. Experimental result on the image `fingerprint' shows that the proposed construction of arbitrary subspace is a more effective approach. In addition, experimental results on the three kinds of images show that the proposed evaluation method of digital image scrambling degree is more effective than other three frequently-used methods. In this way, we can quickly find the best number of scrambling transformation in order to get the best image scrambling performance, rather than randomly set the number of scrambling transformation.",
